# sym_var_test.am1 and sym_var_part.ah: the line each var is declared on, and
# each label defined on, in the file it is WRITTEN in.  Read off the numbering
# of those two sources and written before the first run; check 2 derives the
# same with awk.
#
# name          line    the shape it is there for
afterblock      18      # a var after a C-style comment block
afterinc        21      # a var after the include returns
alone           12      # a var alone on its line
atend           23      # declared after "variables", so placed at the end of the program
begin           9       # a label, for company
fwdvar          19      # referenced before it is declared
incvar          7       # declared in sym_var_part.ah
initd           15      # an initialized var
last            24      # a label after the vars
pairone         14      # the first of two on one line
pairtwo         14      # the second of two on one line
withcomment     13      # a trailing "//" comment after it
